+# DRAFT — notice to the recipient of a withdrawn returns case
+
+**For JML to review and send through an authorised channel. Not sent by Claude.**
+In the demonstration the recipient is a GEX test account (Sander de Vries, ABN AMRO Structured
+Lending); if this case is ever shared with a real lender, adapt the wording and send it from HamburgOne.
+
+---
+
+**Subject:** North Sea e-Methanol — returns case "Base case (chain)" v1 withdrawn from reliance
+
+Dear Sander,
+
+On 18 November 2026 HamburgOne shared with you, read-only on GreenEarthX, the returns case
+"Base case (chain)" version 1 for North Sea e-Methanol (sha256 `c5de242046c1…`).
+
+We have withdrawn that version from reliance the same day, and your access to it has been revoked.
+Please do not rely on it, or on any copy or export of it you may hold.
+
+**Why.** The techno-economic base case behind it did not price the plant described in our saved Cost
+Basis. It priced a generic methanol-synthesis train that bought hydrogen at a model default instead of
+including our 120 MW electrolyser, applied a location for the Netherlands rather than Germany, ignored our
+stated 10 % contingency, and relied on engineering defaults that were not listed as assumptions. Its
+figures (project IRR −10.0 %, fixed capital €175.3M) are therefore not a fair statement of the project.
+
+**What happens next.**
+- The calculation has been corrected to price the saved Cost Basis line by line, with every remaining
+  default listed.
+- The corrected base case currently shows a CO₂ supply shortfall of about 11,900 t/yr, which we will
+  resolve before anything is published.
+- An independent engineer, instructed by you (reference GEX-TEST-IE-NSEM-001), will review it.
+- Only after that review will we publish a new version, with a reconciliation against version 1, and
+  share it with you.
+
+Copies already downloaded cannot be recalled by the platform; we would be grateful if you marked them
+as superseded.
+
+Kind regards,
+[name, function], HamburgOne
